{%- comment -%}
  AJ Brand shipping — what shipping this brand actually costs, on the PDP.

  A block rather than a hardcoded section so it can be positioned in the theme
  editor against whatever the product page ends up looking like, and removed
  without a deploy.

  All of the reasoning about WHY this is measured rather than written lives in
  `snippets/aj-brand-shipping.liquid`. The short version: shipping on Collective
  is charged per supplier and every supplier prices it differently, so the
  shipping agent measures each one weekly and this renders whatever it found.

  It renders NOTHING for roughly a third of suppliers, and that is the point.
  Nine get more expensive as you add items; six have a free-shipping threshold
  their own catalogue cannot reach. Both would produce a claim that is false.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="aj-brand-shipping-block" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  {%- render 'aj-brand-shipping', product: product -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Brand shipping",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Shows what shipping costs for this product's brand — free, ships-together-free, or how much more to add for free shipping. Measured weekly by the shipping agent. Stays blank for brands where no honest claim can be made."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Brand shipping" }]
}
{% endschema %}
